#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:1
msgid "llvm-gsymutil - GSYM dumping, searching and creating utility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:8
msgid "{program}`llvm-gsymutil` \\[*options*\\] \\[*gsym-files...*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:12
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-gsymutil` is a tool for dumping, searching, and creating GSYM "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:15
msgid ""
"GSYM is a compact file format for debug information, optimized for fast "
"lookups. It can represent address ranges, line tables, and inline info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:18
msgid "The tool has three main modes of operation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:20
msgid ""
"**Dump Mode**: If one or more GSYM files are specified as arguments without "
"any lookup options, the tool dumps all the information contained in the "
"specified files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:23
msgid ""
"**Lookup Mode**: If a single GSYM file is specified along with one or more "
"{option}`--address` options (or {option}`--addresses-from-stdin`), the tool "
"performs lookups for the specified addresses in the GSYM file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:26
msgid ""
"**Convert Mode**: If the {option}`--convert` option is specified, the tool "
"converts the specified ELF or Mach-O file into GSYM format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:29
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:32
msgid "Display information on the various flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:36
msgid "Display the version of the tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:40
msgid "Enable verbose logging and encoding details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:44
msgid ""
"Convert the specified file to the GSYM format. Supported files include ELF "
"and Mach-O files. The tool will convert their debug info (DWARF) and symbol "
"table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:49
msgid ""
"Specify a separate file to read the symbol table from during GSYM "
"conversion. Use when the symbol table and debug info are in separate files. "
"Matching architectures are selected automatically for universal binaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:55
msgid ""
"When used with {option}`--convert`, encodes merged function information for "
"functions in debug info that have matching address ranges. Without this "
"option, one function per unique address range will be emitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:58
msgid ""
"When used with {option}`--address` or {option}`--addresses-from-stdin`, all "
"merged functions for a particular address will be displayed. Without this "
"option, only one function will be displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:64
msgid ""
"Load call site info from DWARF, if available. This flag only has an impact "
"when converting to gsym. When using llvm-gsymutil to lookup addresses, any "
"callsite information will automatically be displayed without this flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:70
msgid ""
"Process debug information for the specified CPU architecture only. "
"Architectures may be specified by name or by number. This option can be "
"specified multiple times, once for each desired architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:76
msgid ""
"Specify the path where the converted GSYM file will be saved. When not "
"specified, a '.gsym' extension will be appended to the file name specified "
"in the {option}`--convert` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:82
msgid ""
"Verify the generated GSYM file against the information in the file that was "
"converted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:87
msgid ""
"Specify the maximum number (n) of simultaneous threads to use when "
"converting files to GSYM. Defaults to the number of cores on the current "
"machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:92
msgid ""
"Specify the size in bytes of the size the final GSYM file should be "
"segmented into. This allows GSYM files to be split across multiple files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:97
msgid "Do not output warnings about the debug information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:101
msgid "Lookup an address in a GSYM file. Can be specified multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:105
msgid ""
"Lookup addresses in a GSYM file that are read from stdin. Each input line is "
"expected to be of the following format: `<addr> <gsym-path>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:110
msgid "Output a categorized summary of errors into the JSON file specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:114
msgid ""
"When used with {option}`--address` or {option}`--addresses-from-stdin` and "
"{option}`--merged-functions`, filters the merged functions output to only "
"show functions matching any of the specified regex patterns. Can be "
"specified multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:121
msgid "Set the GSYM output version (1 or 2). Default: 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-gsymutil.md:125
msgid ""
"Print the size of each section in the input GSYM file(s). Format can be "
"`text` (default), `json`, or `pretty-json`. Calling this option without "
"arguments is equivalent to `--statistics=text`."
msgstr ""

